// @run
// @log 1
// @hint Intentionally-unused function `_inlineLen`
// @hint Intentionally-unused function `_i32Only`
// THE PLAIN `string` FIELD WAS THE ONE STRING-CARRYING FIELD CODE THAT RESERVED NOTHING.
//
// `collectA`'s struct-FIELD table pass re-derives the collection PRESENCE flags from the
// interned field codes, because a field's own type is never a standalone `TypeRef` the arena
// scan can see — the whole `{v: string}` shape is ONE name. Every string-carrying code in that
// loop forces `aUsed`: code 6/31 the string list, code 4/18 the i32 list's shared backing,
// code 19/29 the map's string keys, code 20 the `string | null` niche. Code 3 — a field whose
// type IS `string` — did not, and it is the one that names a string directly.
//
// Without it `aTypeIdx = mNextType`: an index that is never allocated but is usually still IN
// RANGE, so the field silently named whatever heap type sat there. Measured on `231e137c` it
// came out a FUNC type, and `array.len` over that is INVALID WASM at `vl check` rc 0
// (171 bytes written, then a validation failure at the `.length`).
//
// THE BOUNDARY IS THE POINT. A DECLARED `type S = { v: string }` already reserved through its
// own `TypeDecl` route — `function _len(b: S) { return b.v.length }` is 405 bytes before AND
// after, as is the two-level `Outer -> Inner -> string` — so only the spellings that reach the
// emitter as an INLINE shape were exposed: this file's annotation shape, and the union VARIANT
// shape in `plain-string-variant-field-reservation.vl`.
//
// BYSTANDER TWIN: `print("live")` instead of `print(1)` makes this row pass on master
// (488 bytes), which is what makes it a RESERVATION miss rather than a lowering one. So the
// module below contains NO string other than the one its annotation mentions, and the
// string-literal control (`const s: S = { v: "abcd" }` + `print(slen(s))`, 439 bytes before
// and after) is deliberately kept OUT of this file — one literal rescues the whole thing.
//
// The fix is flag-only, so its swallow is provably empty: a separate `if`, not an arm of any
// chain, whose only write is an OR into a presence flag.
function _inlineLen(b: { v: string }) { return b.v.length }

// CONTROL — an inline shape with no string field at all: byte-identical across the change
// (168), because no field code in it reserves anything. With the row above it reads 426 after
// and 192 before, so the two shapes compose rather than one masking the other.
function _i32Only(b: { v: i32 }) { return b.v }

print(1)
